Equal-iteration control (prob_4, run_alns maxIters=3000, seed 7, 1 thread):
  REGRET=0 PACK=0 -> 6,032,474 in 9.6s
  REGRET=8 PACK=0 -> 7,404,850 in 24.4s
  REGRET=8 PACK=60 -> 7,264,779 in 26.1s
  REGRET=3 PACK=0 -> 8,164,369 in 18.1s
=> cost-based/regret insertion is worse PER ITERATION and 2-2.5x slower.
   Mechanism: insertBest scans strided days from the release day and stops at
   maxCand candidates, so it misses insertGreedy's event-driven phase 2 and
   its unconditional phase-3 completeness sweep, i.e. it finds LATER entries.
   First-feasible-earliest already minimises the inserted block's own
   tardiness exactly, which is 78-96% of the P4-P6 objective, so there is no
   headroom for a cost tie-break on the same axis. AXIS REFUTED.

Equal-iteration control for the tardy-seed first claim (same protocol):
